---
title: Mojito sorbet
servings: 8
yield: 1%l
tags: [dessert, frozen, lime]
source: https://github.com/Gunde/recipes
---

Make a syrup: bring @water{200%ml} and @sugar{90%g} to the boil in a #saucepan{} and stir until every grain has dissolved. Take it off the heat, add the zest of a @lime{1} and the @mint leaves{handful}, and steep for ~{1%hour}.

When the syrup has cooled to about 50 °C, stir in the @honey{100%ml} until it dissolves. Let it reach room temperature, then chill in the fridge until cold.

Stir in the @lime juice{200%ml}, @soda water{300%ml} and @light rum{2%tbsp}, then churn in an #ice cream maker{} following its instructions. Freeze until firm.
